rules_rust fix: declare the x86_64-unknown-linux-musl triple.

`rust/platform/triple_mappings.bzl`: rules_rust supports musl ABIs for other
architectures but does not declare `x86_64-unknown-linux-musl`, so
`@rules_rust//rust/platform:x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` does not exist and every
generated crate select fails to resolve. The home services build a static musl
binary with the hermetic zig cc_toolchain; this triple is only used by that
image target (the platform carries the extra `musl` constraint), so declaring
it next to the other Linux triples is unambiguous.

--- a/rust/platform/triple_mappings.bzl
+++ b/rust/platform/triple_mappings.bzl
@@ -81,6 +81,9 @@
     "x86_64-apple-ios-macabi": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "x86_64-linux-android": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "x86_64-unknown-freebsd": _support(std = True, host_tools = True),
+    # Static service images (solutions/wakegrant). The target platform carries
+    # @zig_0_14_1//:musl, so this triple never selects the glibc toolchain.
+    "x86_64-unknown-linux-musl": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "x86_64-unknown-fuchsia": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "x86_64-unknown-none": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "x86_64-unknown-uefi": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
